  "worked_solution": "A vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D\u2286{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $\u03c8(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y}=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each vector field.\n\n- Vector field I doesn't have a stream function. The partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}=3,\\,\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y} & =-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y}=3+(-2y)\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II doesn't have a stream function. The partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}=1,\\,\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y} & =2xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y}=1+2xy\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III has a stream function. Indeed, the partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}=2x,\\,\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y} & =-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y}=2x+(-2x)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
